  message: "STILL CORRECTLY DEFERRED, and now for a measured reason rather than an absent\none. Partial MEAS-1 landed 2026-08-17 (numbers and caveats on WI-kazas):\n\n  small 33 s | medium 119 s | large 201 s | MONOREPO 489 s\n\nThis item's gate is WI-kazas's third band, \"tens of minutes on a monorepo ->\nfile-level memoization earns its keep\". The monorepo cell came in at 8.2\nminutes. That is the second band, which selects WI-zagij (package scoping), not\nthis. I am not stretching 8.2 minutes into \"tens of minutes\" to unblock the more\ninteresting item — the whole point of the gate was to stop exactly that.\n\nWHAT WOULD ACTUALLY UNGATE THIS, both already filed:\n- WI-rukaz: a ~14.6k-file Java repo running >60 min with the bottleneck\n  unlocated. If that reproduces it IS the \"tens of minutes\" cell and this item\n  ungates immediately. Worth measuring before building anything here.\n- The analysis-vs-linking split of a cold run. This item already names the\n  linkers as the \"irreducible remainder\"; if linking dominates, NEITHER this\n  nor WI-zagij helps much and the target is the linker stage instead. The\n  per-pass timers in AnalysisRun make this cheap.\n\nONE PIECE OF EVIDENCE FOR THIS ITEM'S SOUNDNESS HAZARD, observed incidentally.\nThe cache's `<analyzer_identity>` segment hashes the CONTENT of every installed\nhypergumbo_* .py file, so adding a single comment to edge_types.py moves it\n(09f205d121a3680a -> c0784fc9dcd9a62a, and back on revert). That is the correct\nbehaviour for that segment and it is NOT what makes smart-test slow — smart-test\nuses the pipx $STABLE_HG, whose identity is constant. It is recorded here only\nbecause it demonstrates the \"COMPLETE KEY\" hazard this item warns about is real\nand already being handled at whole-tree granularity: a per-file key has to carry\nevery one of those inputs, and the failure mode is a silent stale hit."  # 71ac
